            "review_title": "Review at An's Saigon",
            "review_text": "Cssi C\nSan Francisco, California17 contributions\n0\nOur Hearts and our Tummies are FULL! Yay\nJan 2025 • Couples\nChefs Table! What an absolute treat and stunning environment - I took lots of pictures! . Winning combination of great food, such warm and personalized hospitality and team, and lovely location with garden and gorgeous room and gardens. \n\nWe have been happily eating at so many great places - but An's Saigon was the STAR of our trip. \n\nWe very much enjoyed our experience at the Chefs Table. Arrived in a beautiful hidden courtyard - and loved seeing the herb garden, the various fermentations that Chef and his team creates. We are seated at a lovely room and the magic begins - with our own garden at our seat.\n\nThe short rib and the special fragrant rice was delicious. The squid and dried bamboo dish was creative, the deconstructed shrimp roll was clever. Desserts with the cotton candy spun in front of us enveloping an apricot was so much fun.\n\nWe want to come back for the a la Carte menu - which has some very delicious looking local favorites too. And their coffee. Must come back.\n\nLocation is in District 2 - which is quieter and just a short grab/taxi from our hotel villa so it worked out nicely.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nMake sure to book in advance. Tip - go onto facebook mesenger - and email - and ask about any openings - it's easy to get a table that way.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten January 10, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
